<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; Christian Prayer" cic="CCC 2558-2649" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What is prayer according to the Catechism, and how did Saint Thérèse of Lisieux define it?</li>
<li>Who takes the initiative in prayer: us or God? How does the story of the Samaritan woman illustrate this?</li>
<li>Name the five principal forms of prayer and describe each in one sentence.</li>
<li>What are the three expressions of prayer, and how do they relate to each other?</li>
<li>Name four fundamental attitudes for Christian prayer and identify the parable or Scripture passage that illustrates each.</li>
<li>What are the four main enemies of prayer according to the Catechism? How should we respond to each?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. Describe your current prayer routine. What form or expression of prayer comes most naturally to you? What feels difficult or foreign?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Be honest. If you do not have a routine, say so. The important thing is to start from where you are — God meets us in reality, not in ideals.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Have you ever experienced a moment when you felt God was truly listening to you or present to you in prayer? What was it like?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">If it has never happened, do not worry. Prayer does not depend on feelings. Saint John of the Cross reminds us that dryness can be a deeper form of union.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. Is there a person or situation you have been praying for persistently (like Saint Monica for Augustine)? Or is there something you have stopped praying for because the answer seemed to take too long?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Monica prayed for seventeen years. Her story teaches us that God's delays are not denials. Write the name or situation here — and recommit to praying for it this week.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. The Catechism says prayer is a &laquo;battle.&raquo; What is currently the biggest obstacle in your prayer life? (Distractions, dryness, lack of time, doubts, acedia, or something else?)</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Identifying the obstacle honestly is the first step. What one small, concrete change could you make this week to face that obstacle?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. If you knew with absolute certainty that God is looking at you right now with infinite love, what would you say to him? What would you most want to share?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Write the first thing that comes to mind. Do not overthink it. This is the seed of your personal prayer.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">6. Of the five forms of prayer (blessing/adoration, petition, intercession, thanksgiving, praise), make a personal assessment: which do you practice most, and which do you most neglect? Design one small exercise for the form you neglect — something you can try this week.</p>
<p class="question-block__p">For example, if you neglect thanksgiving, promise to name three specific things you are grateful for each evening before bed. Write your exercise here.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

